      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, please have a seat. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Well, I'm here because... I keep hearing this man's voice. It comes right out of the garage vents at the shop, and sometimes from under the hood of the cars I'm working on. It's as clear as you sitting right there, telling me not to trust my husband, and warning me not to touch certain cars. \n\nWhich is a real problem because I'm a mechanic. If I don't touch the cars, I can't do my job, right? I've been working on cars since I took some classes at the community college. My instructor back then had this beautiful 1969 Mustang, but the alternator was always giving him trouble. He used to say a machine has a soul, you just have to listen to it. I bought this really nice socket set for that class, still use it today actually. Snap-on. Costs an arm and a leg, but the warranty is incredible. My husband complained about the price when I bought them, but he doesn't understand quality tools. He bought this cheap blender last week that broke on the very first try. \n\nAnyway, I'm sorry, what did you ask me? Oh, right, why I'm here. Yeah, the man in the vents just keeps talking to me about my husband and the cars.",
