      "doctor_question": "How long have you been hearing this man's voice?",
      "targeted_symptom": "psychotic_symptoms_duration",
      "patient_response": "It's been... gosh, about ten months now, I think. Both the voice and that feeling that someone is tracking me. Ten months is a long time, you know? It started right around the time the shop got that new air compressor. It's a Quincy, really powerful, but man, the vibration on that thing is something else. It rattles the whole back wall if you don't bolt it down right. I told the shop manager, I said, \"Dave, you gotta put rubber mounts under those feet or it's gonna drive us all crazy.\" He didn't listen, of course. Dave never listens. He thinks because he wears a tie to a mechanic shop he knows better than the people turning the wrenches. He actually spilled coffee on his tie last Tuesday and tried to get it out with brake cleaner. I could have told him that would ruin the silk, but... well, he wouldn't have listened anyway. Brake cleaner is amazing for getting grease off a rotor, though. Evaporates in seconds. But yeah, ten months of this guy talking to me.",
