    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have you heard the voice at times when your mood felt completely normal?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_3",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, actually... there was this stretch of a few weeks where things were pretty quiet for me. I was sleeping a lot more, just resting, you know? Not making all those huge plans to overhaul everything like I do when I'm really revved up. But even during that quiet time, I still heard the voice coming from the garage vents. And I still knew for a fact that my husband and my boss were tracking me. \n\nSpeaking of my boss, Dave, he actually installed these new security cameras at the shop right around then. He claimed it was for \"insurance purposes,\" but they're these crazy 4K high-definition dome cameras with infrared night vision. You know how infrared works, right? It picks up heat signatures. I got really into reading about thermal imaging a while back when I was trying to figure out the best way to diagnose a misfiring cylinder. Because sometimes a standard laser thermometer just doesn't cut it when you're trying to find a dead hole on an exhaust manifold. You point the laser, but if your hand shakes and you're off by even half an inch, you get a completely wrong temperature reading. So thermal imaging is way better for that. But those cameras Dave bought... totally excessive for a basic auto shop. He said he got a deal on them at Costco. Have you been to Costco on a Saturday? It's an absolute madhouse. You go in for a rotisserie chicken and you come out with a kayak and a fifty-pound bag of flour. \n\nWait, what were we talking about? Oh, right, my mood. Yeah, even when I was feeling totally normal and just resting, the voice was definitely still there, and the tracking didn't stop.",
