      "doctor_question": "Have you used any recreational drugs, alcohol, or medications around the time these experiences started or recently?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, no drugs or anything like that. I don't really drink either, maybe a beer at a barbecue once in a blue moon, but that's it. I don't take any medications. Actually, wait, I did take some ibuprofen a couple weeks ago because I tweaked my shoulder. \n\nIt was the stupidest thing, too. I was trying to break loose a lug nut on this F-250 that some guy had completely over-torqued. You know those pneumatic impact wrenches? They're great, but if someone just sits there and hammers on a lug nut with a one-inch drive gun, it basically cold-welds the thing to the stud. I had a three-foot breaker bar on it and I was basically hanging my entire body weight off the end of it, and when it finally popped loose, my shoulder just went *crunch*. It's the rotator cuff, I'm pretty sure. The supraspinatus tendon gets pinched right under the acromion if you're not careful. I read this whole article about shoulder biomechanics in mechanics, actually. It's a huge problem in the industry because you spend half your life working with your arms above your head under a lift. My uncle had to have double shoulder surgery because of it. He used to build custom hot rods out in Nevada. Beautiful cars, mostly old Fords. He had this '32 coupe... chopped top, suicide doors, the works. Painted it this unbelievable candy apple red. He mixed the paint himself.\n\nBut yeah, no drugs or anything like that. Just the ibuprofen for my shoulder.",
